      "data": {
        "text": "**Choosing Provider**\n\nI've decided to move forward with Google Cloud Monitoring as the metric data provider for this Python script. This choice provides a concrete foundation to build upon. Now I will focus on defining the queries.\n\n\n**Defining the Structure**\n\nNow I'm structuring the `filter_metric_dimensions.py` script. I'm focusing on defining a function to query metric data with parameters for project ID, metric type, resource and metric labels, and time windows. I've incorporated the `google-cloud-monitoring` library's `monitoring_v3` client to interact with the Google Cloud Monitoring API. The imports and function structure are now the primary focus.\n\n\n",
